  "summary": "A phase-free X-spider with n inputs connected to a phase-free Z-spider with m outputs becomes a complete bipartite graph.",
  "description": "The general form of [strong complementarity](../bialgebra/): an X-spider with n inputs connected to a Z-spider with m outputs is equal to n Z-spiders and m X-spiders connected as a complete bipartite graph, with scalar $\\sqrt{2}^{(n-1)(m-1)}$. It follows from the 2-by-2 bialgebra rule and spider fusion.\n\nIn the special cases where n or m is 0 or 1 it reduces to state copying and identity removal.",
